  "id": "diary-method",
  "term": "diary method",
  "definition": "The diary method is a research approach in which participants record their experiences or states repeatedly over a short period, such as each day. In this source, it is used to study day-to-day changes and reduce errors that can happen when people try to remember past experiences later.",
